## Model card
- **Name:** Cat Jam Free (stealth model)
- **Short description:** Stealth reasoning model optimized for coding and agentic workflows, with low-latency inference, tool calling, and structured JSON outputs. Released under "Stealth" provider; exact vendor/identity unconfirmed (sometimes self-reports as LitterBox AI in probes). Alias: Cat Jam / cat-jam-free.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen (`opencode/cat-jam-free` or similar free tier), Vercel AI Gateway (`stealth/cat-jam`), Command Code. Supports OpenAI Chat Completions / Responses API and Anthropic Messages API compatible endpoints.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-10-12 (OpenCode free release; Vercel AI Gateway ~2026-10-15); knowledge cutoff not publicly disclosed.
- **IDs:** `stealth/cat-jam` (Vercel); `cat-jam-free` (OpenCode / models.dev). Free-tier ID exists on OpenCode Zen.
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 total (1M); max output 131,072. Verified via models.dev toml and Vercel AI Gateway provider table.
- **Modalities:** text in; text out; reasoning yes (effort levels: low/medium/high/xhigh/max); tool calls yes; structured JSON mode yes. No image/video/audio/PDF input.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-16):** Free (input/output/cached $0). Free-tier privacy caveat: prompts may be retained for safety (up to ~30 days on some hosts); Zero Data Retention not available; some hosts note possible use for training/model improvement.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary (open_weights = false); params total/active and MoE status unknown.
